course: dictionary
lesson: 12269
title: Continually: again and again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Continually means again and again, very often, with short breaks in between. «The phone continually rang, so Sam could not finish his homework.» The phone did not ring once. It rang, stopped, and rang again, many times.
explain: Sometimes continually means all the time, without stopping. «The Earth is continually moving, turning as it circles the Sun.» Scientists use the word this way to show that something keeps happening.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. «He continually interrupts when I speak» shows the action happens again and again, and it sounds annoying. Ask yourself: does this happen over and over? If yes, continually fits.
explain: Be careful not to mix it up with continuously. Continuously means without any break at all. Continually often means again and again, with gaps in between. Both can describe something that never seems to stop, so check the sentence carefully.
fact: Continually is an adverb, so it tells you how often or how something happens.
fact: «Continually» means again and again, very often, with short breaks in between.
fact: It can also mean all the time, without stopping, as in «the Earth is continually moving».
fact: It is often confused with «continuously», which always means without a break.
fact: When a word describes something that repeats a lot, the reader can often tell it is annoying or tiring.
exercise: «She continually forgot her lunch box.» What does continually mean here? | Very slowly | Never, not at all | *Again and again, very often | Only once, on Monday
exercise: «The fridge hums continually all night.» Which word means nearly the same as continually? | Quietly | Once | Sadly | *Non-stop
exercise: Ben says continually and continuously mean exactly the same. Is he right? | No, continually is a colour | Yes, they mean exactly the same in every sentence | No, continually is only used for animals | *Partly: continuously always means without a break, but continually often means again and again with gaps
test: «My little brother continually asks why the sky is blue.» What does continually show about the brother? | He asks once and then is quiet forever | He never asks any questions | He is asleep most of the day | *He asks again and again, very often
test: Mum says, «You have ___ left the door open!» Which word fits best? | *continually | continue | contain | curly
exam: Which sentence uses continually to mean again and again, with short breaks? | *«The bell rang continually, every few minutes, all through the lesson.» | «The bread was continually soft and warm.» | «He ate one biscuit continually.» | «The sun set continually on Monday.»
